export const ENGLISH_LESSON = `# Unit 3: Working in an office

## Vocabulary

| Word | Meaning | Translation |
| --- | --- | --- |
| deadline | the time by which a task must be finished | date limite |
| colleague | a person you work with | collègue |
| schedule | a plan of when things will happen | emploi du temps |
| promotion | a move to a more important job | promotion |

## Reading: A busy Monday

Sarah arrives at the office at eight o'clock every morning. Her manager usually sets up a meeting with the whole team on Mondays.
Today the team must finish the report before the deadline. Sarah checks her schedule and answers her emails quickly.
Her colleague Tom often helps her when the work becomes stressful. They follow up on every request from their clients.
After lunch, the manager announces that Sarah will get a promotion next month. Everyone congratulates her.
Good communication helps a team to meet its deadlines. A clear schedule reduces stress and improves productivity.

## Phrasal verbs

- set up – to arrange or organise something
- follow up – to find out more or take further action
- put off – to delay doing something
- fill in – to do someone's job for a short time

The meeting was put off until Friday because the manager was ill. Tom filled in for Sarah while she was on holiday.

## Grammar: present simple

We use the present simple for habits and routines. With he, she and it, we add -s to the verb: she works, he answers.
Negatives use does not with he, she and it: Tom does not work on Sundays.
`;

export const FRENCH_LESSON = `# Leçon 5 : Les fruits et légumes

## Vocabulaire

- la pomme : un fruit rond, rouge ou vert
- la carotte : un légume orange et long
- le marché : un lieu où on achète des produits frais
- la saison : une période de l'année

## Texte

Chaque samedi, Marie va au marché avec sa grand-mère. Elle achète des pommes, des carottes et des tomates.
Les fruits de saison sont moins chers et plus savoureux. Au marché, les vendeurs proposent souvent de goûter leurs produits.
Marie prépare une soupe de carottes pour le dîner. Sa grand-mère prépare une tarte aux pommes délicieuse.
Le marché signifie un lieu de rencontre pour les habitants du quartier.
`;

export const ARABIC_LESSON = `# الدرس الثاني: في المدرسة

## المفردات

- المعلم: الشخص الذي يدرّس التلاميذ
- الفصل: الغرفة التي يدرس فيها التلاميذ
- الواجب: العمل الذي يقوم به التلميذ في البيت
- المكتبة: مكان فيه كتب كثيرة

## النص

يذهب أحمد إلى المدرسة كل صباح. يحب أحمد معلم اللغة العربية كثيرًا.
في الفصل، يقرأ التلاميذ القصص ويكتبون الجمل. بعد الدرس، يذهب أحمد إلى المكتبة ليقرأ كتابًا.
في المساء، يكتب أحمد الواجب ويراجع دروسه. المعلم يشجع التلاميذ على القراءة كل يوم.
`;
